+ *   +0x00 deflated EA      +0x04 inflated EA
+ *   +0x08 deflated size    +0x0C inflated size
+ *   +0x10 work-to-do counter EA | type (bit 0: 1 = inflate, 0 = stored copy)
+ *   +0x14 SPURS event flag EA   +0x18 u16 event-flag bits
+ *
+ * The task decrements the counter when an element is done and sets the bits
+ * once it reaches zero. Neither the ANY2ANY queue algorithm nor that task's
+ * pop path is modelled faithfully here -- the task woke, found nothing, and
+ * the title parsed its archives still compressed -- so service the element on
+ * the host: raw-deflate inflate (stb_image's zlib), counter, event flag. It is
+ * also far cheaper than running inflate as lifted SPU code. Only an element
+ * of exactly that shape, naming a registered event flag, is taken this way;
